#~ msgid "Fractional distillation is used for the separation of two or more miscible<br>liquids for which the difference in boiling points is less than 25K.<br>Methanol boils at 65&deg;C and ethanol boils at 78&deg;C."
#~ msgstr "Fractional distillation is used for the separation of two or more miscible<br>liquids for which the difference in boiling points is less than 25K.<br>Methanol boils at 65&deg;C and ethanol boils at 78&deg;C."

#~ msgid "Simple distillation is used for the separation of a mixture containing two<br/>miscible liquids that boil without decomposition and have sufficient<br/>difference(>25k) in their boiling points. At 56&deg;C acetone boils and the</br>vapours are collected in a RB flask and water is left behind in the flask."
#~ msgstr "Simple distillation is used for the separation of a mixture containing two<br/>miscible liquids that boil without decomposition and have sufficient<br/>difference(>25k) in their boiling points. At 56&deg;C acetone boils and the</br>vapours are collected in a RB flask and water is left behind in the flask."

#~ msgid "The denser particles forced to the bottom and the<br>lighter particles stay at the top when spin rapidly."
