#~ msgid "The denser liquid at the bottom forms the lower layer and the lighter<br>liquid forms the top layer. This indicates water is denser than oil."
#~ msgstr "The denser liquid at the bottom forms the lower layer and the lighter<br>liquid forms the top layer. This indicates water is denser than oil."

#~ msgid "Simple distillation is used for the separation of a mixture containing two<br>miscible liquids that boil without decomposition and have sufficient<br/>difference (>25k) in their boiling points. At 36&deg;C pentane boils and the<br/>vapours are collected in a RB flask and heptane (bp - 98&deg;C) is left</br>behind in the flask."
