#~ msgid "Simple distillation is used for the separation of a mixture containing two<br/>miscible liquids that boil without decomposition and have sufficient<br/>difference (>25k) in their boiling points. At 69&deg;C hexane boils and the<br/>vapours are collected in a RB flask and toluene (bp - 111&deg;C) is left</br>behind in the flask."
#~ msgstr "Simple distillation is used for the separation of a mixture containing two<br/>miscible liquids that boil without decomposition and have sufficient<br/>difference (>25k) in their boiling points. At 69&deg;C hexane boils and the<br/>vapours are collected in a RB flask and toluene (bp - 111&deg;C) is left</br>behind in the flask."

#~ msgid "Fractional distillation is used for the separation of two or more miscible<br>liquids for which the difference in boiling points is less than 25K.<br>Acetone boils at 56&deg;C and hexane boils at 69&deg;C."
#~ msgstr "Fractional distillation is used for the separation of two or more miscible<br>liquids for which the difference in boiling points is less than 25K.<br>Acetone boils at 56&deg;C and hexane boils at 69&deg;C."

#~ msgid "Fractional distillation is used for the separation of two or more miscible<br>liquids for which the difference in boiling points is less than 25K.<br>2-Propanol boils at 82.5&deg;C and 2-Butanol boils at 99.5&deg;C."
